# Working agreement

## Stack
- Use a .NET 8 class library + xUnit test project. Nothing else.
- Never add a CLI, HTTP endpoint, UI, or NuGet package I did not ask for.

## Code style
- Use 'decimal' for all money. Never use 'double' or 'float'.
- Use records for data. One public entry point for the behaviour (the calculator); helpers stay private or internal.
- No placeholder code, no TODOs, no extra design "just in case".
- Refactor existing code only when the current requirement demands it.

## Process
- TDD: write the failing tests for the current requirement first, then the smallest implementation that passes.
- Implement only what the current message asks. Do not build ahead of the requirement, even if you can guess what comes next.
- Do not tidy or refactor code unrelated to the current requirement.
- If a requirement is ambiguous, stop and ask me one question instead of guessing.
- Be ruthless in your approach while getting the steps/task done.

## Boundaries
- I run git. Never commit, never push. Propose a one-line commit message when tests are green.
- Don't edit the README; I will be adding the content for it.
